{"chunk_id": "ed150dddd06c", "text": "After Sita enters the fire to prove her purity, the fire\u2011god Agni (here called Pavaka or Vibhabasu) rises from the extinguished pyre in visible form, carrying her unharmed. Radiant and adorned, Sita is returned to Rama. Agni publicly declares before all that she has remained completely faithful\u2014her thoughts fixed only on Rama despite Ravana\u2019s captivity, threats, and temptations. The divine testimony confirms that she is without sin and must not be reproached. Rama, hearing this, is filled with joy but explains his earlier harshness: the ordeal was necessary to demonstrate Sita\u2019s innocence before the world, since public suspicion would otherwise stain both her and his kingship. The moment resolves the moral and emotional crisis following the war, with a god\u2019s authority restoring Sita\u2019s honor.\nAfter Sita emerges unharmed from the fire, the Fire God declares her purity and returns her to Rama, who explains the trial was for public opinion.\nThemes: trial by fire, public duty vs personal feeling, divine testimony, chastity and honor", "vector": [0.013980143703520298, -0.024838892742991447, -0.0096353217959404, -0.0028419899754226208, -0.025050513446331024, -0.0016590674640610814, -0.024071769788861275, 0.0005381429218687117, -0.024865346029400826, -0.012617840431630611, 0.011652324348688126, 0.00921208132058382, 0.02285495586693287, 0.005525264889001846, -0.009410475380718708, -0.0073405671864748, 0.041186533868312836, 0.007624931633472443, 0.019178058952093124, -0.01491920743137598, -0.013074145652353764, -0.010303246788680553, -0.027140259742736816, 0.023357553407549858, -0.035472795367240906, 0.0007377766305580735, 0.01677088253200054, -0.039705194532871246, 0.012875751592218876, -0.010409057140350342, -0.011374573223292828, -0.02087101899087429, -0.016255058348178864, -0.007406698539853096, -0.019006118178367615, -0.00419602682814002, -0.019349999725818634, -0.011870557442307472, 0.0047184638679027